cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RRM-1 in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "RRM-1: A Reference Architecture and Benchmark for Embodied Reasoning"
abstract: >-
  RRM-1 is a modular embodied-reasoning architecture and reproducible benchmark.
  Perception feeds a persistent semantic world model, a reasoner plans over
  symbolic state, a deterministic verifier gates every action, and a
  vision-language-action policy converts abstract verbs into motion. The
  benchmark measures whether an explicit world model, predictive planning and an
  independent safety verifier improve task success, recovery and safety over
  end-to-end VLA control.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Abolade
    given-names: Ore
repository-code: "https://github.com/o-abolade/rrm"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
